# rm441, the dark drawer (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm441
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_dunstan_plankham
written_by codex
title the dark drawer
fits stage=adult|old
prefers honesty=guarded talk=quiet
traits temper=short talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk checks_a_neat_drawer_by_touch_with_eyes_shut
likes crisp_apples swimming tidy_house warm_rain
dislikes deep_mud salt_wind
fears a_moved_seal a_foot_lost_in_deep_mud
hopes a_clean_sill_after_rain a_towel_where_it_belongs
topics home +0.5 pastimes +0.4 gossip -0.5
styles comfort=practical gossip=withheld refuse=terse tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps a drawer in such order that its contents can be found in darkness, guards private business carefully, and rates a dry towel above most luxuries.

words
oath! = Salt on the hinge | Anvil in the mud
saying! = Let the hand find what the mouth won't name | A seal belongs to its errand
drawercleat = a narrow wooden cleat | a thin stop beneath the drawer
touchrow = my row of small ends | the loose things in their places
towelturn = the rolled towel edge | the end turned underneath
knifeheel = a blunt handle end | a smooth wooden heel
applecheek = the cool apple skin | a thin red cheek
stonepip = a dark little brown pip | a hard point of seed
swimbend = the turn out of deep water | a sheltered bit near the bank
sealcloth = a plain dry wrapping | an oilcloth square
mudmark = a black thumb of mud | a streak of soft clay
saltflare = a rough white patch | a little crust of brine

any
opinion @1 city for 1 : I can get what I need inside these walls without explaining every choice to some wolf on a distant road. I'd keep that convenience.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : A grand door may stay shut longer than a small one, even to an honest knock. I've no admiration for the extra lock.
opinion @1 strangers against 1 : A strange paw can move something by an inch and walk away. I'll put my business away before I speak.
opinion @1 sump for 1 : On a Sump stair, giving the next wolf one clean foothold generally says all the welcome that's needed.
opinion @1 watch against 1 : The Watch makes a great deal of knowing what everybody carries. I've a liking for getting home with my own small things private.
opinion @1 festivals against 1 : I can't keep an account of my pockets and enjoy festival music at the same time. I'll hear it from my own doorway.

grown
line @1 greet : Everything's put away. Speak.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : We may exchange ordinary words at this distance.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Early enough to see the drawer empty before anything's stirred.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Keep your hands there in the patch I can see.
line @5 greet [self.working=yes] : Just closing something. You can speak now.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come round to the familiar end of the table.
line @1 again.open : Back at the same drawer with no time to disturb it.
line @1 greet.return : I heard. Your greeting's accounted for.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Familiar voice. No need for a second call.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : I can answer with one hand occupied.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Heard from a clean patch of quiet.
line @1 farewell : Don't leave your loose things at the turn.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll do the putting away here.
line @1 react.news : Put down exactly what happened.
line @1 react.news.new : That wasn't in the place I expected.
line @1 react.news.known : I had the outline laid away.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Did the first paw actually hold the matter?
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : A towel and a dry seat would give that house something small to offer a caller.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : A tidy piece of good news. I can spare space for that.
line @1 answer.how : I could find the towel with my eyes closed. Fine.
line @1 ask.how : Have you much left unsettled where you live?
line @1 sympathise : Can't put everything right by getting the drawer tidy.
line @1 reassure : You may sit here till your hands know where to go.
line @1 decline : I'd be breaking the seal on business that's not mine to open.
line @1 accept_decline : Good. Yours stays on your side.
line @1 thank : You left my things in easier reach.
line @1 deflect_thanks : Set any loose thing you borrow down in its proper place.
line @1 preclose : There's one loose end for me to attend to.
line @1 accept_preclose : I've no call to hold you here.
line @1 ack : Sits right.
scene blindrow
when topic=home self.likes=tidy_house
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My fingers can settle on the right thing in my drawer with the shutters closed.
b : Even a small thing? | Why practise without light?
a : Especially small things. I can feel the little wood stop where the loose ones go. | A drawer can't stay well lit all the way through a night.

scene apple
when topic=food self.likes=crisp_apples
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like an apple I can hear break through its own skin.
b : Would you test it in the shop? | Does it keep as well?
a : I'd buy it before taking a bite. Other wolves' goods stay whole in my hands. | I keep the firm ones separate from the bruised ones. Neither gets to choose its neighbours.

scene linen
when topic=pastimes self.likes=swimming
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I roll a dry towel with one end tucked back into its own turn.
b : To keep the sand out? | How would you recognise it among other towels?
a : To keep that one dry place. Cold fingers like to find something they can trust. | By the feel of the fold. I don't care to unroll somebody else's over my wet feet.

scene warmrain
when topic=weather self.likes=warm_rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A warm shower makes the dust outside the sill easy to wipe in one pass.
b : Wouldn't you have to dry it again? | Don't you like watching the street instead?
a : One pass now, a dry cloth after. Better than grinding at a week's worth of hardened mud. | Sometimes. I'd rather look out over a clean edge while I do it.

scene deepclay
when topic=land self.dislikes=deep_mud
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I test a dark patch of mud before putting my heel anywhere close to its middle.
b : With what? | Does the colour tell you enough?
a : A loose twig. If the twig loses half its length I choose the next patch. | No. A shiny skin can look the same over a shallow scrape or mud reaching almost to my ankle.

scene salt
when topic=weather self.dislikes=salt_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Salt gets into a drawer runner if the wind comes in sideways.
b : Do you shut the window? | Can you hear the grit?
a : Before a real blow, yes. A window's there to be a choice. | A scratch under the soft sound of wood. Worth wiping before it cuts a groove.

scene sealedword
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An errand can be perfectly honest without wanting anybody's nose under the fold.
b : Would you say where a letter went? | Doesn't a seal make you curious?
a : To the ear it was given for. The rest belongs in my pocket. | Curious enough to check it's unbroken. I need nothing further from the question.

scene drywork
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The first thing with a paper errand is getting the paper under decent cover.
b : Before finding out the destination? | What if a stranger asks to see the seal?
a : On a wet day, yes. An unreadable address doesn't narrow the search much. | I'd ask what business the stranger had with my fold. Then I'd decide what answer was due.

scene tightroom
when topic=home self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In a Sump room a drawer that opens too far puts the whole household in somebody's lap.
b : Would you shorten it? | How much should it open?
a : I'd put a stop on the runner. Most useful things are better for knowing where to finish. | Enough to reach the last clean square of cloth without pulling all the others into the air.

scene swimtime
when topic=pastimes self.likes=swimming
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep my fingers open just before leaving the water.
b : For balance? | To find the ledge?
a : To see if I'm still feeling the ends properly. A numb grip is a bad thing to guess at. | That's next. First I'd check my fingers can feel what the eyes are expecting.

scene cityjob
when topic=smalltalk self.apprentice=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm learning to give an answer no longer than the instruction asked for.
b : Is that hard? | How do you ask for more detail?
a : Easy to give too little. Easier to let out something that had no business coming into the answer. | Say what I understand and name the bit still missing. No need for noise about the rest.

scene privatekin
when topic=smalltalk self.neighbour
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd pass a dry packet to #self.neighbour# with the fold turned in.
b : Doesn't the neighbour need to read it? | Would you tie the string tight?
a : The intended reader can turn a packet over. Nobody else needs the first look on the stairs. | Securely. A desperate knot only invites somebody to take a knife to it.

scene purseprice
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I count the small purchase in the light before it goes in the pocket.
b : Afraid of losing a coin? | Are your pockets labelled too?
a : Afraid of wasting somebody's evening looking for a coin I never put there. | I know what I expect on each side. A label would be more information than I mean to give.

scene tidyfaith
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's a clean corner in a chapel that requires nothing of me but sitting still.
b : Do you carry anything there? | What if it's occupied?
a : Just what I came with. No reason to put private matters on a bench. | Then the next wolf can have that quiet corner. There'll be somewhere else to sit in good time.

scene rainsign
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A wet sleeve gives a clean towel a new purpose, then makes it want a place to dry.
b : Have you always room to hang it? | Why be so exact?
a : I've one peg kept for it. I don't want to clear a shelf with both hands full of rain. | Because it's my space to put right. A small order belongs to whoever has to live in it.

scene marks
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dream of opening a drawer that has kept every object exactly as I left it but shifted the drawer itself across the city.
b : Could you find it? | Would that annoy you?
a : I could tell you whether it was mine with one reach inside. First I'd have to get there. | Considerably. I keep some of my pleasures very near the surface.

scene roadwalk
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I don't open my bag halfway along a muddy stretch.
b : What might fall out? | Even for food?
a : Whatever it is I least want in the mud. Bags have a very exact sense of a bad occasion. | I can wait till I reach a dry patch. A gritty apple would be a poor payment for haste.

scene rimlight
when topic=day here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At night a bit of white cloth inside the drawer saves me looking for the handle of a dark tool.
b : I thought you found things by touch? | What if the cloth gets moved?
a : Most nights I do. My eyes may as well take a turn looking after the fingers occasionally. | Then the drawer feels wrong and I put it right. Quiet work for the last few minutes before bed.

story wrongturn [topic=memories]
  : I once changed the end where I kept a little bundle of cord. For a whole week my paw landed at the old place first.
  : At last I set a clean apple in the old place. I was determined to teach my hand a useful distinction.
  b : Did the apple cure the habit?
  : I ate it and went back to keeping the cord there. The hand had a perfectly sound arrangement to begin with.

story swimcloth [topic=pastimes self.likes=swimming]
  : I rolled a towel tight and put it high on a dry rock. I'd forgotten to shake out a small pebble tucked inside.
  : After swimming I rolled the towel open. The stone came out quite dry and landed straight in a puddle.
  b : Did it give you a shower?
  : One spatter on the sole of my foot. I put the pebble back with the bits of bank that hadn't arranged themselves a private towel.

story wholepeel [topic=food self.likes=crisp_apples]
  : I cut an apple peel in a single long piece and placed the curl on my sill.
  : The peel tightened into a little circle. I'd been trying to leave a mark showing where the draught came in.
  b : Did it show the draught?
  : Showed the peel wanted to curl. I tried again with a dry thread and ate a very good apple.

rule @drawer
when concept=bark self.likes=tidy_house
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Runner's clear. Don't shove it past the stop. | Loose ends into their own row.

rule @swim
when concept=bark self.likes=swimming
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Towel above the high wet mark. | Get a dry grip before you step up.

rule @wet
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Wrap the paper while the fold's dry. | Leave the seal inside the cloth.

rule @dark
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One clean white edge left showing. | Last loose thing away before the lamp.

dlg @1 resident.hub : I've set my work aside. You can state your business.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : I know where your voice belongs, #topic.player#.
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Keep outside reach of the drawer. We can speak across it.
dlg @4 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Your voice doesn't need a lamp. It reaches me quite clearly where you're standing.
dlg @1 resident.job : I keep what's given me dry and in its proper place. That's all I care to say of my work.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : This bit is out in plain sight. #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : See your things home with the folds dry.
graft @darkdrawer resident.hub
choice What could you find without opening your eyes? -> darkdrawer
node darkdrawer
say The drawer stop, then the folded towel. Behind the towel there's a row of small things. If one is out of place, my hand has to go looking, so I notice.
choice Will you show me the whole row? -> darkdrawer_more
choice Let the drawer close. -> hub
node darkdrawer_more
say The towel and the stop were what I meant to show you. You have what you need to try making a sensible drawer at your own place. Mine can close now.
choice Let the drawer close. -> hub
choice Leave the folds alone. -> bye
